   "text": "The image shows three separate components: a gadolinium ion, a DTPA ligand and two meglumine molecules. This is gadopentetate dimeglumine.\n\n**DTPA ligand (top).** Three nitrogens are linked by two \u2013CH2CH2\u2013 bridges.\n- The left nitrogen carries one CH2COOH and one CH2COO\u207b.\n- The central nitrogen carries one CH2COO\u207b.\n- The right nitrogen carries one CH2COOH and one CH2COO\u207b.\n- This gives three carboxylates and two free acids.\n\n**Meglumine (two identical copies).** Each is CH3\u2013NH\u2013CH2 followed by four CH(OH) groups and a terminal CH2OH.\n- Stereochemistry follows the hashes and wedges, taken from the NH end: hashed OH, hashed OH, hashed OH, then wedged OH.\n- I assigned each centre from the drawn geometry, treating the implicit hydrogen as pointing opposite the drawn OH bond.\n- This gives CNC[C@H](O)[C@@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@H](O)CO, which agrees with the standard N-methyl-D-glucamine SMILES as I remember it.\n\n**Metal.** Gd\u00b3\u207a is written as [Gd+3].\n\nSMILES: [Gd+3].OC(=O)CN(CC([O-])=O)CCN(CC([O-])=O)CCN(CC(O)=O)CC([O-])=O.CNC[C@H](O)[C@@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@H](O)CO.CNC[C@H](O)[C@@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@H](O)CO"
